rchase and redemption and information on investment yields of savings notes appear in the Treasury Bulletins of March 1967 and June 1968; and the Annual Report of the Secretary of the Treasury for fiscal year 1974.\n[In millions of dollars. Source: Monthly Statement of the Public Debt of the United States; Market Analysis Section, United States Savings Bonds Division]\n| Savings bonds: | Savings bonds: | Savings bonds: | Savings bonds: | Savings bonds: | Savings bonds: | Savings bonds: |\n| Savings notes | 862 | 538 | 1400 | 1070 | 330 | - |\n1 Sales and redemption figures include exchange of minor amounts of (1) matured series E bonds for series G and K bonds from May 1951 through April 1957; (2) series F and bonds for series H bonds beginning January 1960; and (3) U.S. savings notes for series H bonds beginning January 1972; however, they exclude exchanges of series E bonds for series H and HH bonds.\nTable SBN-2.--Sales and Redemptions by Period, All Series of Savings Bonds and Notes Combined\n[In millions of dollars. Source: Monthly Statement of the Public Debt of the United States; Market Analysis Section, United States Savings Bonds Division]\nU.S. SAVINGS BONDS AND NOTES\n[In millions of dollars. Source: Monthly Statement of the Public Debt of the United States; Market Analysis Section, United States Savings Bonds Division]\nNote.--Series E and EE Include U.S. savings notes (Freedom Shares) on sale from May 1, 1967, through June 30, 1970, to E bond buyers.\n| End of month > Unnamed: 0_level_1 | Total privately held > Unnamed: 1_level_1 | Commercial banks 2 > Unnamed: 2_level_1 | Total > Unnamed: 3_level_1 | Individuals 3 > Total | Individuals 3 > Savings bonds 4 | Individuals 3 > Other securities | Nonbank investors > Insurance companies | Nonbank investors > Money market funds | Nonbank investors > Corporations | Nonbank investors > State and local governments 6 | Nonbank investors > Foreign and International 7 | Nonbank investors > Other Investors 8 |\n1 U.